  "description": "A fully renovated split-level on a quiet no-through street in Pennsauken Township, with 2,016 square feet across two levels. The upper level opens into a light-filled living room with an oversized window, a wainscoted accent wall and recessed lighting that carries through the home, all over newly custom-stained hardwood floors. The kitchen just off the living room is white and new: Calacatta quartz counters, a fresh backsplash, stainless appliances, luxury vinyl plank flooring and a breakfast bar with stools, with the dining room adjacent. Three bedrooms sit down the hall, each with a large closet and a brushed-nickel ceiling fan, and one connects Jack-and-Jill style to the renovated full bathroom finished with a gray tile floor, Calacatta shower tile and a white vanity. Downstairs is a large walkout family room with luxury vinyl plank, recessed lighting, an under-stair storage closet and a new sliding glass door out to the patio; the opposite side of the lower level is a very large partially finished space. Mechanical and electrical work runs throughout, including a new 150-amp panel and service line, new meter and disconnect boxes, new outlets and switches, and new smoke and carbon monoxide detectors. Outside there is a new charcoal roof, black shutters and exterior lighting, a new stone driveway and stone-and-brick walkway, and a wood-fenced 0.21-acre lot with a patio and front porch. Natural gas forced-air heat, central air, public water and public sewer.",
